Package: grip
Type: Package
Title: Graph Drawing with Intelligent Placement (GRIP)
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: 
    c(person("Pawel", "Gajer", , "pgajer@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
      person("Jonathan", "Zheng", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
             comment = "Author and copyright holder of MIT-licensed s_gd2 code adapted for the metric-MDS SGD backend"),
      person("Daniel", "Hangan", role = "ctb",
             comment = "Author of the SGD-MDS implementation in his scikit-learn fork adapted for the metric-MDS SGD backend"),
      person("The scikit-learn developers", role = "cph",
             comment = "Copyright holders of BSD-3-Clause code adapted from Daniel Hangan's scikit-learn fork for the metric-MDS SGD backend"))
Description: Implements GRIP multiscale graph layout with a unified choice
    between hop-count and geometry-aware edge-length graph metrics in 2D and
    3D. Provides layout scoring, candidate
    comparison, multiscale trace diagnostics, synthetic graph families,
    and advanced experimental geodesic-KK utilities for weighted-layout
    evaluation and polish. Based on Gajer and Kobourov (2002)
    <doi:10.7155/jgaa.00052> and Gajer, Goodrich and Kobourov (2004)
    <doi:10.1016/j.comgeo.2004.03.014>. Includes derived graph datasets from
    the SuiteSparse Matrix Collection, with source attribution and
    transformation metadata.
